// HΛRM FILE: README.hrm
// PURPOSE: Overview of the Harmonia OS interactive console
// ROLE: This file provides a high-level description of the Harmonia OS project,
//       a cross‑platform interactive shell for the Harmonia DSL, aligned with RI1 principles.

HARMONIA_OS_OVERVIEW {
    VERSION: 0.1
    STATUS: DRAFT
    DESCRIPTION: 
        The Harmonia OS interactive console is designed as a lightweight, offline tool
        for writing and exploring Harmonia DSL code. It emphasises non‑coercive,
        recursive, and harmonic interactions. Developers can use this console to
        experiment with DSL scripts, receive real‑time feedback, and visualize
        recursive structures.
    REFERENCE:
        See Roadmap.hrm for technical design notes.
}

// END FILE — README.hrm
